----- stdout -----
Generate IDLs and Rust, JavaScript, and Dart clients.

Discovers Pina programs below `EXAMPLES_DIR`, optionally filters them with repeatable --example arguments, writes IDLs, and renders all three client targets. The command fails when a requested example does not exist or a renderer exits unsuccessfully.

Usage: pina codama generate [OPTIONS]

Options:
      --examples-dir <DIR>
          Directory containing Pina program crates. Defaults to `examples`

      --idls-dir <DIR>
          Directory for generated Codama IDL JSON files. Defaults to `codama/idls`

      --rust-out <DIR>
          Directory for generated Rust client crates. Defaults to `codama/clients/rust`

      --js-out <DIR>
          Directory for generated JavaScript client packages. Defaults to `codama/clients/js`

      --dart-out <DIR>
          Directory for the generated Dart client package. Defaults to `codama/clients/dart`

      --example <NAME>
          Program name to generate. Repeat to select multiple programs. When omitted, every program below --examples-dir is generated

      --npx <COMMAND>
          Executable used to invoke the Codama JavaScript renderers. Defaults to `npx`

  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

Examples:
  pina codama generate
  pina codama generate --example counter_program --example todo_program
  pina codama generate --examples-dir ./programs --idls-dir ./idls \
                --rust-out ./clients/rust --js-out ./clients/js --dart-out ./clients/dart

Requirements:
  The selected --npx executable, or the default pnpm fallback, must be available when JavaScript and Dart client rendering runs.

